.SH BUGS
HTTP/2 and HTTP/3 are not spoken; HTTP/1.1 over TLS 1.3 is.
Passwords are HTTP Basic: a browser keeps one until it is closed,
and there is no logging out.
Rules for paths that did not exist when
.I httpd
started match by name alone; restart it after making a protected
directory on a host that folds case.
Certificates are ECDSA P-256 only, and there is no ACME client to keep
one renewed.
